# Module DB File Style Guide

Conventions for database table definitions in app modules. The table is the
**source of truth** for the module: the DTO (`<module>.dto.ts`) derives its
Zod schemas from it, and row types flow from there through the router to the
client. PostgreSQL is the only supported dialect.

## Conventions

- Import enum-like constants from shared constants: `@appname/shared/modules/<module>/<module>.constants`.
- Import auth tables for foreign keys: `import { users, organizations, members } from "@m5kdev/backend/modules/auth/auth.db"`.
- Define tables with `appDatabaseSchema.table(...)` from `@m5kdev/backend/base/database.schema`, so every app table lives in the app-owned PostgreSQL schema (`DATABASE_SCHEMA`). Column builders come from `drizzle-orm/pg-core`.
- Use `uuidv4` as the default for string IDs via `.$default(uuidv4)`.
- Represent booleans with `boolean("col")` and `.notNull().default(false)` when the value is required.
- Represent timestamps with `timestamp(..., { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" })`.
  - `createdAt`: `timestamp("created_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" }).notNull().$default(() => new Date())`
  - `updatedAt`: `timestamp("updated_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" })`
  - `deletedAt`: `timestamp("deleted_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" })`
- JSON values use native JSONB: `jsonbValue("col")` from `@m5kdev/backend/base/database.schema`, typed with `.$type<...>()`. Scalar lists use native arrays: `text("tags").array().$default(() => []).$type<string[]>()`. Do not store JSON or arrays as serialized text.
- Use `references(() => otherTable.id, { onDelete: "cascade" })` for non-nullable FKs and `{ onDelete: "set null" }` for nullable FKs.
- Composite join tables define primary keys with `primaryKey({ columns: [t.aId, t.bId] })`.
- Table names are plural; column names are snake_case at DB level, camelCase in code.
- Inline union types are acceptable for simple status columns: `.$type<"draft" | "published">()`.
- Include `deletedAt` when the module needs soft deletes — `queryList`
  automatically excludes soft-deleted rows when the column exists.

## Registration and migrations

- Register every new table in `apps/server/src/schema.ts` with a plain
  re-export: `export { posts } from "./modules/posts/posts.db";`. The schema
  file is maintained by hand — there is no generation step.
- After changing tables, run `drizzle:generate`. It writes a migration to
  `drizzle-postgresql/` from the table definitions. Never hand-write or edit
  migration SQL and never edit files under `drizzle-postgresql/meta/`.
- Every table change must be backward-compatible with the code currently in
  Production. Read `.cursor/rules/database-migrations.mdc` before changing a
  table: removing or renaming a field here generates a destructive migration.

## File Location

```
apps/<app>/server/src/modules/<module>/<module>.db.ts
```

## Example

```typescript
import { appDatabaseSchema, jsonbValue } from "@m5kdev/backend/base/database.schema";
import { members, organizations, users } from "@m5kdev/backend/modules/auth/auth.db";
import { boolean, primaryKey, text, timestamp } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";
import { v4 as uuidv4 } from "uuid";

export const posts = appDatabaseSchema.table("posts", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey().$default(uuidv4),
  authorUserId: text("author_user_id").references(() => users.id, {
    onDelete: "set null",
  }),
  memberId: text("member_id").references(() => members.id, {
    onDelete: "set null",
  }),
  organizationId: text("organization_id").references(() => organizations.id, {
    onDelete: "set null",
  }),
  title: text("title").notNull(),
  slug: text("slug").notNull().unique(),
  excerpt: text("excerpt"),
  content: text("content").notNull(),
  status: text("status").$type<"draft" | "published">().notNull().default("draft"),
  tags: text("tags")
    .array()
    .$default(() => [])
    .$type<string[]>(),
  metadata: jsonbValue("metadata").$type<Record<string, unknown>>(),
  publishedAt: timestamp("published_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" }),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" })
    .notNull()
    .$default(() => new Date()),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" }),
  deletedAt: timestamp("deleted_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" }),
});

export const postsUsers = appDatabaseSchema.table(
  "posts_users",
  {
    userId: text("user_id")
      .notNull()
      .references(() => users.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
    postId: text("post_id")
      .notNull()
      .references(() => posts.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
    pinned: boolean("pinned").notNull().default(false),
  },
  (t) => [primaryKey({ columns: [t.userId, t.postId] })]
);
```
